WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:21.000
La Elaha Ella Allah (There is no god but One God)

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Alhamdu Lillah, Wa Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah Wahdahu La Shareeka Lah.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
We praise God and we bear witness there is only One God.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.000
God is doing everything.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.000
And this is the conclusion that we must reach

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.000
if we are to be saved.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
That God is doing everything is a quality of God.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
If you don't know this quality, then you don't know God.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.000
And this is why the Quran is full of those verses

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.000
talking about people who do believe in God

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
but they're going to Hell

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.000
because they do not know God as He really is.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
In Sura 8, verse 17,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.000
we're told that God...

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.000
There was the appearance of a battle

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:23.000
with a small handful of believers fighting a big huge army of disbelievers.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:29.000
And the believers were busy running around and stabbing and throwing arrows and shooting, thinking they are fighting,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:36.000
but the verse tells us that God is the One who's fighting; God is the One who did the killing and the throwing of the arrows.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.000
God is doing everything.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
We only do the decision to be with God or not.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:55.000
And the whole design of this life is to effect a test for each one of us.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.000
This whole life is a test,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.000
nothing else.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.000
And we read in Sura 51, verse 56 that God created this whole universe,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.000
created us just to worship Him alone.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Anything else are just the means for provision,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:18.000
the jobs, what you do to go to school to find work, develop your talents or whatever.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.000
It's just an outside appearance to provide for you,

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.000
give you the dollars, the food, the roof over your head and so on.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:31.000
But the main job, when you wake up in the morning, my main job today is to worship God Alone.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
And to observe my duties towards God.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:40.000
All those duties, of course, are designed for our own benefit to develop and grow our soul

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.000
through the prayers, the fasting and so on.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.000
But the whole world is designed for a test

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:53.000
in that a person is required to pray before sunrise, for example

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.000
in order for his or her soul to grow and develop.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.000
And some person may say oh, the sun is rising too early

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.000
4 o'clock in the morning, you know, in July and August.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.000
They complain.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.000
But the sunrise is at 4 o'clock, you know, I'm not gonna get up at 3:30 to do the morning prayer.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.000
So, God says ok. I'm gonna make it rise at 7.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.000
And God designed the earth.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.000
It's a little bit lopsided, so it will go up and down in front of the Sun

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.000
in this way creating the winter and the short day and the long day.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:37.000
And God will say ok. Now, the Sun is rising at 7 o'clock. Are you going to pray the morning prayer before sunrise?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.000
See, God designed the test this way.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.000
And God nullifies the excuses of everybody

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.000
in order to see who is going to make it to the Highest Heaven

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.000
and that is the person who's gonna pray before sunrise no matter what time the sun rises.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000
And also to assure the place of those who are going to the

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.000
lowest pit of Hell

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.000
because even when the sun rises at 7 o'clock, they will not pray the morning before sunrise.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:15.000
So, you can see the range of the time of sunrise and how God did it to sift out the ranks.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.000
The people who will pray when the sun rises at 6.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.000
And people who will pray when it rises at 6:30.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.000
And people who do the morning prayer when it rises at a quarter of seven.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.000
So, there'll always be dropouts.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.000
And there will be those who pray no matter what time the sun rises.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.000
3 in the morning, they'll be up by 2:30

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.000
and they'll do the morning prayer and go back to sleep, but they will do it.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:46.000
People will say I'm gonna fast in Ramadan 16 hours? The day is 16 hours long

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.000
and I'm gonna eat no food, no water for 16 hours and it's so hot!

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.000
God says ok. I'm gonna cool it down for you. I'm gonna make it 7 hours.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.000
And God does that.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:02.000
So, you can see that the fasting days range from 7 hours, 9 hours

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.000
of cool day

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.000
to 16 hours of hot days.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.000
And you can see the test going on

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.000
and you can see the dropouts.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.000
Some people will fast even if the day is 20 hours in August.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.000
And nobody dies anyway from that. It's good for you, takes down your blood pressure,

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.000
reduces your weight and all that.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:30.000
And nobody dies if he or she fasts for two consecutive days.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.000
But there are people who will fast even if the day is 20 hours long.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.000
For the last 19 years,

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.000
we've been giving the Muslim world evidence

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.000
that they have deviated,

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.000
that we must adhere to the Quran Alone

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.000
and we've been showing them the verses in Quran.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:00.000
So they said well, who is this Rashad Khalifa? He's an ignorant person

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.000
He's never been to Azhar.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.000
And he's duping the ignorant people who don't know anything about Islam.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.000
They wrote this.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.000
They published it. They lectured and so on.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:15.000
He's a science man. He is not a religious man.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.000
If you hear it from a scholar,

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.000
from Azhar,

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.000
then, you can you know, they wrote that Rashad is ignorant.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.000
He doesn't have a religious degree.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.000
He's not from the Azhar.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.000
And he's deceiving the ignorant people.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:32.000
And God said ok, I'm gonna nullify,

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.000
like the long day, the sunrise at 7,

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.000
He said ok, I'm gonna produce for you the best Azhar scholar.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.000
And he's sitting right with us right now. He's not a usual Azhar scholar.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:53.000
He is one in a long time that was the first of his class in the freshmen, sophomore, junior and senior years.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:57.000
He's not a common Azhar person.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
He didn't have a connection.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:05.000
A lot of people in the Azhar have connections with the dean or the president of the university and they pass and so on,

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:12.000
but there are special students who get this degrees and they graduate with the first honors, they call it.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:17.000
And he's one of those, one of the unusual students.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:20.000
And when he graduated the first of his class,

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.000
he was hired in the university

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.000
and he taught at the university

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:31.000
and he made his Ph.D. on the same subject that we preach here in this mosque

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:35.000
that the prophet will not intercede on your behalf on the day of judgement,

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.000
that the prophets are human beings who made mistakes.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:42.000
And they gave him the Ph.D. with the highest degree ever in the Azhar.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:42.000
So, he's not just...

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:47.000
God said I'm gonna give you an Azhar man, not just an Azhar man, I'm gonna give you the best.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:55.000
And so, so, he goes out and he teaches and he steals the students from all the other professors.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:00.000
I mean, these are facts that are recorded now in the headlines of the front pages

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.000
that came out in the last month as he was in prison

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.000
and our powerful Fãtehah got him out, ALHAMDULILLAH (Praise be to God).

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:13.000
But he would go and teach in the senior class

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:19.000
and then he will go to teach the next period, will be in the sophomore class.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:22.000
The students from the senior class will follow him to the sophomore class

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.000
and the professor of the senior class will complain,

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.000
where are my kids? Where are the students?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.000
Well, they followed Subhi Mansour to the Sophomore class.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:34.000
So, he raised a lot of jealousy within the university

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:38.000
besides the fact that he was preaching exactly...

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.000
it's identical to what we've learned here

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.000
in this mosque and what we've been preaching.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:47.000
And the enemies of Quran, the enemies of God went crazy

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.000
because God nullified their excuse.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.000
He said ok. You don't like Rashad Khalifa who's a chemist,

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.000
Here's an Azhar man, one of your own

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.000
and one of your best.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.000
And he is preaching the same thing.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.000
He discovered the truth.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:05.000
And I don't know where did God hide him from Satan.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.000
You know, because Satan monopolized all those Azhar people.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.000
He escaped somehow. God protected him.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:16.000
So, he was supposed to give the KHUTBA today, but he refused. He said I wanna see your system first.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.000
Then, I will give the KHUTBA.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:25.000
Also, he wants to increase his mastership of the English language which he does very well.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.000
You know, he really surprised me.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:31.000
But we have now this newspaper saying

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.000
how did he get the Ph.D. in this subject?!

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:38.000
Now, they want to put his committee on trial.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:42.000
Why did they give him the Ph.D.? How did that happen?

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.000
And these happen to be the leaders of the Sunna Institute.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:50.000
I mean, the chairman of his Ph.D. committee is now the head of Sunna Institute in Cairo

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:55.000
And he says how did I do that?!

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.000
They just can't figure it out,

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.000
but he is a living proof of God's power.

00:010:01.000 --> 00:010:04.000
